# Prologue (spec §2): a year ago, the falling out. Then tonight, Dinda's call.
# Budget: 1.5k Indonesian words, about 10 minutes.

@conversation index chapter=Prolog chapter.en=Prologue title="Setahun Lalu" title.en="A Year Ago" checkpoint
@scene VN bg=bg_seawall_night.webp music=bgm_low_tide.mp3 ambience=amb_sea_night.mp3 day=0 time=21:40 textbox=nvl

narration
  id: Tanggul Pluit. Setahun yang lalu.
  en: The Pluit seawall. A year ago.
narration
  id: Dari atas sini, Jakarta kelihatan kayak orang yang lagi nahan napas.{w} Gedung-gedung nyala di belakang, laut hitam di depan, dan tembok beton di tengah-tengahnya.
  en: From up here, Jakarta looks like it's holding its breath.{w} Towers lit up behind us, black sea in front, and a concrete wall in between.
narration
  id: Sekar duduk di atas tembok itu, kaki menggantung ke sisi laut, seolah jatuh itu sesuatu yang cuma terjadi ke orang lain.
  en: Sekar sits on top of that wall, legs dangling over the sea side, like falling is something that only happens to other people.
narration
  id: Gue berdiri di belakangnya, megangin dua gelas es teh plastik yang udah mulai keringetan.
  en: I'm standing behind her, holding two plastic cups of iced tea that have started to sweat.

stage
  textbox adv
  show sekar:laugh right transition=slide_left duration=600
  show raka:smirk left transition=slide_right duration=600

sekar:laugh [right]
  id: Dengerin dulu. Serius, dengerin sampai habis, baru boleh ngeledek.
  en: Just listen. Seriously, hear the whole thing first, then you can make fun of me.
raka:smirk [left]
  id: Gue belum ngomong apa-apa.
  en: I haven't said anything.
sekar:smile
  id: Muka lo udah ngomong dari tadi, Ka.
  en: Your face has been talking the whole time, Ka.
raka:smirk
  id: Muka gue emang begini dari lahir.
  en: My face has looked like this since birth.
sekar:laugh
  id: Iya, dan dari lahir juga lo nyebelin.
  en: Yeah, and you've been annoying since birth too.

narration
  id: Gue naik ke tembok dan duduk di sebelahnya, agak jauh dari pinggir. Gue nggak pernah suka ketinggian. Dia tahu, makanya dia selalu ngajak ke sini.
  en: I climb up and sit next to her, a little further from the edge. I've never liked heights. She knows, which is why she always drags me here.
narration
  id: Kita kenal dari SMA. Dia yang pertama nyapa, di hari pertama, karena gue satu-satunya anak yang bawa headphone segede helm.
  en: We met in high school. She talked to me first, on the first day, because I was the only kid with headphones the size of a helmet.
narration
  id: Lima tahun kemudian, dia punya podcast dengan dua ratus pendengar, dan gue tukang edit suaranya yang nggak pernah dibayar.
  en: Five years later, she has a podcast with two hundred listeners, and I'm the unpaid guy who cleans up its audio.

choice BANTER by=sekar:smile
  id: Sekar nyenggol bahu lo.
  en: Sekar bumps your shoulder.
? "Oke. Gue dengerin." | "Okay. I'm listening."
  value listen
? "Dua ratus pendengar, Kar. Sembilan puluhnya bokap lo." | "Two hundred listeners, Kar. Ninety of them are your dad."
  value tease

sekar:laugh [if BANTER == 'tease']
  id: Bokap gue cuma satu orang, ya. Walaupun dia punya tiga akun.
  en: My dad is one person, thank you. Even if he has three accounts.
sekar:smile [if BANTER == 'listen']
  id: Tumben. Catet tanggalnya.
  en: That's a first. Write down the date.

narration
  id: Dia nyodorin HP-nya. Di layar, gelombang suara dari rekaman yang dia ambil sore tadi di Muara Angke.
  en: She holds out her phone. On the screen, the waveform of a recording she made this afternoon in Muara Angke.

sekar:serious
  id: Pak Karta. Nelayan, udah tiga puluh tahun melaut dari dermaga yang sama. Katanya, dulu dari sini sampai Pulau Pari airnya masih bisa buat ngaca.
  en: Pak Karta. A fisherman, thirty years out of the same pier. He says that from here to Pulau Pari, the water used to be clear enough to see your face in.
sekar:serious
  id: Sekarang ada patok-patok di tengah laut. Ada yang bilang itu buat pulau baru. Nggak ada yang pernah nanya ke nelayan.
  en: Now there are stakes driven into the open water. Some people say it's for a new island. Nobody ever asked the fishermen.
raka:neutral
  id: Terus?
  en: And?
sekar:smile
  id: Terus gue mau bikin satu episode penuh soal itu. Bukan obrolan santai kayak biasanya. Yang beneran. Wawancara, data, peta.
  en: And I want to do a whole episode on it. Not the usual chill chat. A real one. Interviews, data, maps.
sekar:laugh
  id: Dan gue butuh orang yang bisa ngedit audio tanpa bikin suara angin kayak pesawat jatuh.
  en: And I need someone who can edit audio without making the wind sound like a plane crash.

narration
  id: Dia nengok ke gue. Matanya nyala kayak tiap kali dia nemu ide yang terlalu besar buat dia sendiri.
  en: She turns to look at me. Her eyes light up the way they always do when she finds an idea too big for one person.

sekar:smile
  id: Sabtu ini. Jam lima pagi, di dermaga Muara Angke. Kapalnya Pak Karta berangkat jam setengah enam. Lo ikut, kan?
  en: This Saturday. Five in the morning, at the Muara Angke pier. Pak Karta's boat leaves at five thirty. You're coming, right?

narration
  id: Ini saatnya ngomong. Gue udah nunda dua minggu.
  en: This is when I tell her. I've put it off for two weeks.

raka:worried
  id: Kar.{w} Gue keterima kerja. Di Bandung.
  en: Kar.{w} I got a job. In Bandung.
sekar:neutral
  id: ...Oh. Wah. Itu bagus, kan? Kapan mulai?
  en: ...Oh. Wow. That's good, right? When do you start?
raka:worried
  id: Senin. Gue berangkat Minggu pagi.
  en: Monday. I leave Sunday morning.

stage
  music none fade=2s

sekar:serious
  id: Minggu ini?
  en: This Sunday?
raka:neutral
  id: Iya.
  en: Yeah.
sekar:serious
  id: Lo udah tahu dari kapan?
  en: How long have you known?

narration
  id: Gue nggak jawab. Itu udah jawaban.
  en: I don't answer. That's an answer.

sekar:tired
  id: Dua minggu? Tiga? Kita ketemu tiap hari, Ka. Tiap. Hari.
  en: Two weeks? Three? We see each other every day, Ka. Every. Day.
raka:angry
  id: Ya karena gue tahu bakal kayak gini.
  en: Because I knew it would go like this.
sekar:serious
  id: Kayak gimana? Gue nanya, lo jawab. Itu namanya ngobrol.
  en: Like what? I ask, you answer. That's called talking.
sekar:tired
  id: Lo selalu gitu. Kalau ada yang berat, lo diem, terus tiba-tiba lo udah pergi. Kayak waktu bokap lo. Kayak waktu kuliah.
  en: You always do this. When something gets heavy, you go quiet, and then suddenly you're gone. Like with your dad. Like with college.

stage
  shake intensity=4

raka:angry
  id: Jangan bawa-bawa bokap gue.
  en: Leave my dad out of this.
sekar:serious
  id: Oke. Terus Sabtu? Lo masih bisa ikut Sabtu. Satu hari. Abis itu lo bebas ke mana aja.
  en: Fine. So, Saturday? You can still come on Saturday. One day. Then you can go wherever you want.

choice FALLOUT by=sekar:serious timeout=12s
  id: Sekar nungguin jawaban.
  en: Sekar is waiting for an answer.
? "Lo bukan jurnalis, Kar. Lo cuma punya mic." | "You're not a journalist, Kar. You just own a mic."
  value cruel
? "Nggak semua orang bisa hidup dari mimpi." | "Not everyone gets to live on dreams."
  value cold
? (Nggak usah jawab.) | (Don't answer.) [default]
  value silent

sekar:scared [if FALLOUT == 'cruel']
  id: ...
  en: ...
sekar:tired [if FALLOUT == 'cruel']
  id: Wow. Oke. Seenggaknya sekarang gue tahu lo mikir apa selama ini.
  en: Wow. Okay. At least now I know what you've been thinking all this time.
sekar:tired [if FALLOUT == 'cold']
  id: Mimpi. Iya. Pak Karta juga mimpi, kali ya. Mimpi lautnya balik.
  en: Dreams. Right. I guess Pak Karta's dreaming too. Dreaming his sea comes back.
sekar:tired [if FALLOUT == 'silent']
  id: Tuh kan. Diem lagi.
  en: See? Quiet again.

stage
  hide sekar transition=fade duration=900

narration
  id: Dia turun dari tembok, ngambil tasnya, dan jalan ke arah motor tanpa nengok.
  en: She climbs down from the wall, grabs her bag and walks toward her scooter without looking back.
narration
  id: Dua gelas es teh masih di tangan gue. Esnya udah cair semua.
  en: Both cups of iced tea are still in my hands. The ice has all melted.
narration
  id: Gue bisa ngejar dia. Gue tahu persis harus ngomong apa.{w} Gue nggak ngejar.
  en: I could go after her. I know exactly what to say.{w} I don't go.

-> p_unsent


@conversation p_unsent chapter=Prolog chapter.en=Prologue title="Belum Terkirim" title.en="Unsent"
